From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:30:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h713: v2: the panel's supply and reset

Describe the V2 panel's power as 0183 does for the bench board: PH19
enables its power switch, so it is the fixed regulator vcc-panel, the
display's power-supply; PH16 is its reset; the lamp is its backlight.
These are the V2 TOC1's panel_power_en and panel_gpio_0, and the lines
U-Boot's V2 tree already drives for its initial-off hold. The panel is
physically the bench's; only the board's supply switch moved from PF6.

Without them the display driver never claimed the supply, so 0184's
ordered power-down at shutdown never ran on the V2. A warm reboot taken
while the HDMI source was away then left the panel lit but black with
every SoC register correct and the TCON test pattern black too, through
warm reboots and U-Boot's 3 s hold, until a power cycle. An ordered
PH19 supply cycle from Linux cleared it live.

regulator-boot-on because U-Boot leaves the panel powered;
off-on-delay-us is the panel's PanelOffTiming1, as on the bench.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713-v2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713-v2.dts
@@ -104,3 +104,37 @@
 /* The HDMI receiver and capture drivers own these from the boot handoff. */
 &audio_bridge { status = "disabled"; };
 &tvtop { status = "disabled"; };
+
+/*
+ * The panel's supply and reset, as U-Boot drives them to bring it up (V2
+ * TOC1: panel_power_en = PH19, panel_gpio_0 = PH16; the bench board's
+ * supply is PF6, 0183). It is the bench's panel; only the board's switch
+ * moved. The display driver keeps the panel up and, at shutdown, takes it
+ * down in order -- lamp, signal, reset, rail -- before the SoC resets
+ * (0184). Without these nodes that never ran on the V2: a warm reboot taken
+ * while the HDMI source was away reset the SoC with the panel powered and
+ * its LVDS lanes driven, and the panel stayed lit but black, through warm
+ * reboots and U-Boot's 3 s initial-off hold, until a power cycle or an
+ * ordered PH19 supply cycle (2026-11-22).
+ */
+/ {
+	reg_panel: regulator-panel {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "vcc-panel";
+		gpio = <&pio 7 19 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;	/* PH19 */
+		enable-active-high;
+		/*
+		 * U-Boot leaves the panel powered: keep it on when this
+		 * registers, instead of driving the enable low.
+		 */
+		regulator-boot-on;
+		/* panel_config.ini PanelOffTiming1: the rail's discharge. */
+		off-on-delay-us = <250000>;
+	};
+};
+
+&display {
+	backlight = <&lamp>;
+	power-supply = <&reg_panel>;
+	panel-reset-gpios = <&pio 7 16 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;	/* PH16 */
+};
